1.USB Webcam:

1. Place the webcam on top of the monitor and adjust it so it faces you.  
2. Connect the webcam to your computer using the USB cable.  
3. Plug the USB connector into an available USB port.  
4. Wait for Windows to automatically detect and install the necessary drivers.  
5. Open the Camera app and verify that the webcam is working.  
6. Test both the video and microphone before use.

2.Wi-Fi Webcam:

1. Place the Wi-Fi webcam in a suitable position.  
2. Connect the webcam to a power source.  
3. Turn on the webcam and use its setup process or companion app to connect it to your Wi-Fi network.  
4. Make sure your computer is connected to the same Wi-Fi network.  
5. Install the webcam’s required software or app on your computer.  
6. Select the webcam in the software and check the video feed.  
7. The webcam is now ready for online classes, meetings, or video calls.
